Linux Mint ARM (unofficial arm64 build of Linux Mint 22.3 "Zena" Cinnamon): virtual machines

What only virtual machines use (the system's first start removes this package on a Raspberry
Pi). Firefox renders in software (/usr/lib/firefox/defaults/pref/mint-arm-vm.js), and the
mint-arm-rosetta service registers Apple's Rosetta for x86-64 Linux programs when the VM runs
under Apple's Virtualization framework with Rosetta sharing enabled. A drop-in for
qemu-guest-agent.service (qemu-guest-agent.service.d/mint-arm.conf) keeps the QEMU guest agent
running when Linux Mint's setup wizard switches to the desktop. /etc/default/grub.d/mint-arm-vm.cfg
makes the VM's screen the kernel's console (console=tty1) instead of the serial port that the
firmware of QEMU's and UTM's virtual machines names, so that the start-up splash shows and an
encrypted system asks for its passphrase on the screen.
